%% System Design for AI — Chapter X.4
%% Diagram: Four Cost Levers of an AI System
%% Source: assets/diagrams/x4-cost-finops/cost-levers.mmd

graph TB
    Request[📨 Incoming request]

    Lever1[Lever 1: Reduce requests<br/>semantic cache + rule-based fallbacks<br/>40-60% of queries don't need the LLM]
    Cache{Semantic<br/>cache hit?}

    Lever2[Lever 2: Prompt caching<br/>system prompt 90% off<br/>free money if your prompt is stable]
    PromptCache[Prompt cache<br/>applied to whatever path]

    Lever3[Lever 3: Model routing<br/>70% to small model, 30% to large<br/>5x cost reduction overall]
    Route{Model router<br/>easy or hard?}
    Cheap[Small model<br/>$0.0005/req<br/>Haiku / 4o-mini / Flash]
    Expensive[Large model<br/>$0.02/req<br/>frontier model]

    Lever4[Lever 4: Reduce tokens per request<br/>shorter prompts, better retrieval,<br/>structured output, stop sequences]

    Response[💬 Response]

    Request --> Cache
    Cache -->|hit| Response
    Cache -->|miss| Route
    Route -->|easy| Cheap
    Route -->|hard| Expensive
    Cheap --> PromptCache
    Expensive --> PromptCache
    PromptCache --> Lever4
    Lever4 --> Response

    style Cache fill:#d4edda,stroke:#155724,stroke-width:2px
    style Route fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#856404,stroke-width:2px
    style Cheap fill:#d4edda,stroke:#155724
    style Expensive fill:#f8d7da,stroke:#721c24
    style PromptCache fill:#cce5ff,stroke:#004085,stroke-width:2px
    style Lever4 fill:#e2d5f1,stroke:#4a148c

    note1[Apply in order:<br/>1 → 4 → 2 → 3<br/>No-quality-loss<br/>levers first]
    note1 -.-> Lever1
